/-!
# Action-weighted Novikov series, localization, and action-field specialization

Let `G` be an additive group with an energy homomorphism `E : G →+ ℝ` and an optional grading
homomorphism `μ : G →+ B`. Adjoining a real action weight produces the extended exponent group
`G × ℝ` with period map `actionPeriod E (g, r) = E g + r` and degree map
`actionDegree μ (g, r) = μ g`. Its degree-zero action monomials `T^r = single (0, r) 1`
(`TauCeti.NovikovSeries.actionMonomial`) shift filtrations without collapsing distinct classes of
equal energy.

Whenever a period homomorphism `N : H →+ ℝ` admits an additive right inverse `ι : ℝ →+ H`
(`∀ r, N (ι r) = r`), the nonnegative section monomials `single (ι r) 1` (`r ≥ 0`) form a
multiplicative submonoid `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.periodSectionSubmonoid`, equal to the submonoid
generated by the strictly positive section monomials (`r > 0`). Every element of this submonoid
becomes a unit in `NovikovSeries R H N`, while every series `z` has support periods bounded below
by some `m` and therefore satisfies `z * single (ι (max (-m) 0)) 1 ∈ nonnegSubring R N`. Hence
`NovikovSeries R H N` is the localization of `nonnegSubring R N` at `periodSectionSubmonoid`
(`TauCeti.NovikovSeries.isLocalization_periodSectionSubmonoid`).

Specializing `ι` to `AddMonoidHom.inr G ℝ` shows that the full action-weighted Novikov ring
`NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)` is the localization of its nonnegative subring at the
nonnegative action monomials `actionSubmonoid R E`
(`TauCeti.NovikovSeries.isLocalization_actionSubmonoid`). Specializing `ι` to `AddMonoidHom.id ℝ`
shows that the real Novikov ring `NovikovSeries R ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)` is likewise the
localization of its nonnegative subring at the positive real monomials
(`TauCeti.NovikovSeries.isLocalization_realActionSubmonoid`).

Before the real extension, the energy-zero residue of `nonnegSubring R E` modulo `posIdeal R E` is
`AddMonoidAlgebra R E.ker` (`TauCeti.NovikovSeries.quotientPosIdealEquiv`). After the real
extension, every `g : G` lifts to the zero-energy element `(g, -E g)`, identifying
`(actionPeriod E).ker` with `G` and
`(nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)) ⧸ (posIdeal R (actionPeriod E))` with the full group ring
`AddMonoidAlgebra R G` (`TauCeti.NovikovSeries.quotientActionPosIdealEquiv`).
When `μ` has infinite range and `R` is nontrivial, an explicit convergent series
`∑' n, T^(m_n) e^(g_n)` in `nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)` meets infinitely many degrees and
shows that the dense graded subalgebra `⨁ b, nonnegGradeBy` is proper
(`TauCeti.NovikovSeries.iSup_nonnegGradeBy_actionDegree_ne_top`).

Finally, a unital ring homomorphism `ρ : R →+* k` induces the continuous action specialization
`TauCeti.NovikovSeries.actionSpecialization ρ E` into `NovikovSeries k ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)` by
pushforward along `actionPeriod E`, restricting to `nonnegSubring` and factoring uniquely through
the localization `actionSubmonoid R E`. When `k` is a field, `NovikovSeries k ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)`
is a field in which every nonzero series factors uniquely at its least exponent `t₀ = b.order` as
`(b.coeff t₀) T^(t₀) (1 + a)` with `a ∈ posIdeal` and `1 + a` invertible by geometric series.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.periodSectionUnit`, `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.nonnegPeriodSection`, and
  `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.periodSectionSubmonoid`: section monomials and their nonnegative
  submonoid for a right inverse `ι : ℝ →+ H` of `N`.
* `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.actionPeriod E` and `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.actionDegree μ`: the period
  `(g, r) ↦ E g + r` and degree `(g, r) ↦ μ g` on `G × ℝ`.
* `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.actionMonomial`, `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.nonnegActionMonomial`, and
  `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.actionSubmonoid`: the degree-zero action monomials `T^r = single (0, r) 1`
  and their nonnegative multiplicative submonoid.
* `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.actionInlRingHom` and `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.actionInlNonnegSubring`: the
  injective continuous inclusion `g ↦ (g, 0)` of base Novikov series.
* `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.actionResidueRingHom` and
  `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.quotientActionPosIdealEquiv`: the energy-zero residue isomorphism
  `(nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E) ⧸ posIdeal R (actionPeriod E)) ≃+* AddMonoidAlgebra R G`.
* `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.actionSpecialization` and
  `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.nonnegActionSpecialization`: pushforward along `actionPeriod E` into
  `NovikovSeries k ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)` and its nonnegative subring.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.periodSectionSubmonoid_eq_closure_pos`: the submonoid of nonnegative
  section monomials coincides with the submonoid generated by strictly positive section monomials.
* `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.isLocalization_periodSectionSubmonoid`,
  `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.isLocalization_actionSubmonoid`, and
  `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.isLocalization_realActionSubmonoid`: localizing `nonnegSubring` at
  nonnegative (or positive) action monomials recovers the full Novikov ring.
* `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.not_isUnit_nonnegActionMonomial`: for `r > 0` over a nontrivial ring,
  `T^r` is not a unit of `nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)`, although it is a unit of
  `NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)`.
* `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.iSup_nonnegGradeBy_actionDegree_ne_top`: when `μ` has infinite image and
  `R` is nontrivial, the dense graded subalgebra of `nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)` is proper.
* `TauCeti.NovikovSeries.exists_posIdeal_eq_single_order_mul_one_add`: leading-term factorization
  `b = single b.order (b.coeff b.order) * (1 + a)` in `NovikovSeries D ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)`.

## References

* K. Fukaya, Y.-G. Oh, H. Ohta, and K. Ono, *Lagrangian Intersection Floer Theory: Anomaly and
  Obstruction*, AMS/IP Studies in Advanced Mathematics 46, 2009, Chapter 2 and Section 6.
* H. Hofer and D. A. Salamon, *Floer homology and Novikov rings*, in *The Floer memorial
  volume*, Progr. Math. 133 (1995), 483–524.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Filter Function Set Topology

namespace TauCeti.NovikovSeries

/-! ### Localization along a period section -/

section PeriodSection

section Group

variable {R H : Type*} [AddGroup H] {N : H →+ ℝ}

/-- For an additive homomorphism `ι : ℝ →+ H`, the monomial `single (ι r) 1` as a unit of
`NovikovSeries R H N`, with inverse `single (ι (-r)) 1`. -/
def periodSectionUnit (R : Type*) [Semiring R] (ι : ℝ →+ H) (r : ℝ) :
    (NovikovSeries R H N)ˣ where
  val := single (ι r) 1
  inv := single (ι (-r)) 1
  val_inv := by
    rw [single_mul_single, ← map_add, add_neg_cancel, map_zero, mul_one, single_zero_one]
  inv_val := by
    rw [single_mul_single, ← map_add, neg_add_cancel, map_zero, mul_one, single_zero_one]

@[simp]
theorem val_periodSectionUnit [Semiring R] (ι : ℝ →+ H) (r : ℝ) :
    ((periodSectionUnit R ι r : (NovikovSeries R H N)ˣ) : NovikovSeries R H N) = single (ι r) 1 :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem val_inv_periodSectionUnit [Semiring R] (ι : ℝ →+ H) (r : ℝ) :
    ((↑(periodSectionUnit R ι r)⁻¹ : (NovikovSeries R H N)ˣ) : NovikovSeries R H N) =
      single (ι (-r)) 1 :=
  (rfl)

variable [Ring R] {ι : ℝ →+ H}

/-- For a right inverse `ι : ℝ →+ H` of `N` and `r ≥ 0`, the nonnegative section monomial
`single (ι r) 1` in `nonnegSubring R N`. -/
def nonnegPeriodSection (R : Type*) [Ring R] (hι : ∀ r, N (ι r) = r) {r : ℝ} (hr : 0 ≤ r) :
    nonnegSubring R N :=
  ⟨single (ι r) 1, single_mem_nonnegSubring (by rw [hι]; exact hr) 1⟩

@[simp]
theorem coe_nonnegPeriodSection (hι : ∀ r, N (ι r) = r) {r : ℝ} (hr : 0 ≤ r) :
    (nonnegPeriodSection R hι hr : NovikovSeries R H N) = single (ι r) 1 :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem nonnegPeriodSection_zero (hι : ∀ r, N (ι r) = r) :
    nonnegPeriodSection R hι le_rfl = 1 := by
  ext1
  simp [nonnegPeriodSection, single_zero_one]

@[simp]
theorem nonnegPeriodSection_add (hι : ∀ r, N (ι r) = r) {r s : ℝ} (hr : 0 ≤ r) (hs : 0 ≤ s) :
    nonnegPeriodSection R hι (add_nonneg hr hs) =
      nonnegPeriodSection R hι hr * nonnegPeriodSection R hι hs := by
  ext1
  simp [nonnegPeriodSection, map_add, single_mul_single]

/-- A section monomial of strictly positive weight lies in `posIdeal R N`. -/
theorem nonnegPeriodSection_mem_posIdeal (hι : ∀ r, N (ι r) = r) {r : ℝ} (hr : 0 < r) :
    nonnegPeriodSection R hι hr.le ∈ posIdeal R N :=
  single_mem_posIdeal (by rw [hι]; exact hr) 1

/-- Over a nontrivial ring, a strictly positive section monomial is not a unit of
`nonnegSubring R N`. -/
theorem not_isUnit_nonnegPeriodSection_of_pos [Nontrivial R] (hι : ∀ r, N (ι r) = r) {r : ℝ}
    (hr : 0 < r) : ¬ IsUnit (nonnegPeriodSection R hι hr.le) :=
  not_isUnit_of_mem_posIdeal (nonnegPeriodSection_mem_posIdeal hι hr)

/-- The multiplicative submonoid of `nonnegSubring R N` formed by the nonnegative section
monomials `{single (ι r) 1 | 0 ≤ r}`. -/
def periodSectionSubmonoid (R : Type*) [Ring R] (hι : ∀ r, N (ι r) = r) :
    Submonoid (nonnegSubring R N) where
  carrier := {a | ∃ (r : ℝ) (hr : 0 ≤ r), a = nonnegPeriodSection R hι hr}
  one_mem' := ⟨0, le_rfl, (nonnegPeriodSection_zero hι).symm⟩
  mul_mem' := by
    rintro _ _ ⟨r, hr, rfl⟩ ⟨s, hs, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨r + s, add_nonneg hr hs, (nonnegPeriodSection_add hι hr hs).symm⟩

@[simp]
theorem mem_periodSectionSubmonoid (hι : ∀ r, N (ι r) = r) {a : nonnegSubring R N} :
    a ∈ periodSectionSubmonoid R hι ↔
      ∃ (r : ℝ) (hr : 0 ≤ r), a = nonnegPeriodSection R hι hr :=
  Iff.rfl

theorem nonnegPeriodSection_mem_periodSectionSubmonoid (hι : ∀ r, N (ι r) = r) {r : ℝ}
    (hr : 0 ≤ r) : nonnegPeriodSection R hι hr ∈ periodSectionSubmonoid R hι :=
  ⟨r, hr, rfl⟩

/-- The submonoid of nonnegative section monomials coincides with the submonoid generated by the
strictly positive section monomials: `r = 0` contributes the identity `1`. -/
theorem periodSectionSubmonoid_eq_closure_pos (hι : ∀ r, N (ι r) = r) :
    periodSectionSubmonoid R hι =
      Submonoid.closure {a | ∃ (r : ℝ) (hr : 0 < r), a = nonnegPeriodSection R hι hr.le} := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (Submonoid.closure_le.2 ?_)
  · rintro _ ⟨r, hr, rfl⟩
    rcases hr.eq_or_lt with rfl | hpos
    · rw [nonnegPeriodSection_zero]
      exact one_mem _
    · exact Submonoid.subset_closure ⟨r, hpos, rfl⟩
  · rintro _ ⟨r, hr, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨r, hr.le, rfl⟩

end Group

section CommRing

variable {R H : Type*} [AddCommGroup H] {N : H →+ ℝ} [CommRing R] {ι : ℝ →+ H}

/-- **Localization of the nonnegative Novikov subring along a period section.** Whenever
`ι : ℝ →+ H` satisfies `∀ r, N (ι r) = r`, `NovikovSeries R H N` is the localization of
`nonnegSubring R N` at `periodSectionSubmonoid R hι`. -/
theorem isLocalization_periodSectionSubmonoid (hι : ∀ r, N (ι r) = r) :
    IsLocalization (periodSectionSubmonoid R hι) (NovikovSeries R H N) := by
  rw [isLocalization_iff]
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rintro ⟨_, r, hr, rfl⟩
    exact (periodSectionUnit R ι r).isUnit
  · intro z
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := z.bddBelow_image_support
    let r : ℝ := max (-m) 0
    have hr : 0 ≤ r := le_max_right _ _
    have hz : z * single (ι r) 1 ∈ nonnegSubring R N := by
      refine mem_nonnegSubring.2 fun h hh => ?_
      by_contra hne
      obtain ⟨u, v, rfl, hu, hv⟩ := exists_add_eq_of_coeff_mul_ne_zero hne
      have hv' : v = ι r :=
        mem_singleton_iff.1 (support_single_subset (ι r) 1 (mem_support.2 hv))
      subst hv'
      have hu' : m ≤ N u := hm ⟨u, mem_support.2 hu, rfl⟩
      have hmr : -m ≤ r := le_max_left _ _
      rw [map_add, hι] at hh
      linarith
    exact ⟨(⟨z * single (ι r) 1, hz⟩,
      ⟨nonnegPeriodSection R hι hr, nonnegPeriodSection_mem_periodSectionSubmonoid hι hr⟩), rfl⟩
  · intro x y hxy
    exact ⟨1, by simp [Subtype.ext hxy]⟩

/-- The canonical ring isomorphism from `Localization (periodSectionSubmonoid R hι)` onto
`NovikovSeries R H N`. -/
def periodSectionLocalizationRingEquiv (hι : ∀ r, N (ι r) = r) :
    Localization (periodSectionSubmonoid R hι) ≃+* NovikovSeries R H N :=
  letI := isLocalization_periodSectionSubmonoid (R := R) hι
  { (IsLocalization.algEquiv (periodSectionSubmonoid R hι)
      (Localization (periodSectionSubmonoid R hι)) (NovikovSeries R H N)).toRingEquiv with }

end CommRing

end PeriodSection

/-! ### The action-weighted extension `G × ℝ` -/

section ActionExtension

variable {S R G B : Type*}

/-- The action-weighted period homomorphism `(g, r) ↦ E g + r` on `G × ℝ`. -/
def actionPeriod [AddZeroClass G] (E : G →+ ℝ) : G × ℝ →+ ℝ :=
  E.comp (.fst G ℝ) + .snd G ℝ

@[simp]
theorem actionPeriod_apply [AddZeroClass G] (E : G →+ ℝ) (p : G × ℝ) :
    actionPeriod E p = E p.1 + p.2 :=
  (rfl)

theorem actionPeriod_inl [AddZeroClass G] (E : G →+ ℝ) (g : G) :
    actionPeriod E (g, 0) = E g := by
  simp [actionPeriod]

theorem actionPeriod_inr [AddZeroClass G] (E : G →+ ℝ) (r : ℝ) :
    actionPeriod E (AddMonoidHom.inr G ℝ r) = r := by
  simp [actionPeriod]

/-- The extended degree homomorphism `(g, r) ↦ μ g` on `G × ℝ`, assigning degree `0` to the real
action factor. -/
def actionDegree [AddZeroClass G] [AddZeroClass B] (μ : G →+ B) : G × ℝ →+ B :=
  μ.comp (.fst G ℝ)

@[simp]
theorem actionDegree_apply [AddZeroClass G] [AddZeroClass B] (μ : G →+ B) (p : G × ℝ) :
    actionDegree μ p = μ p.1 :=
  (rfl)

theorem actionDegree_inr [AddZeroClass G] [AddZeroClass B] (μ : G →+ B) (r : ℝ) :
    actionDegree μ (AddMonoidHom.inr G ℝ r) = 0 :=
  map_zero μ

section Monomials

/-- The degree-zero action monomial `T^r = single (0, r) 1` in
`NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)`. -/
def actionMonomial (R : Type*) [Semiring R] {G : Type*} [AddZeroClass G] (E : G →+ ℝ) (r : ℝ) :
    NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E) :=
  single (0, r) 1

@[simp]
theorem actionMonomial_zero [Semiring R] [AddZeroClass G] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    actionMonomial R E 0 = 1 := by
  change single ((0 : G), (0 : ℝ)) (1 : R) = 1
  exact single_zero_one

@[simp]
theorem actionMonomial_add [Semiring R] [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ) (r s : ℝ) :
    actionMonomial R E (r + s) = actionMonomial R E r * actionMonomial R E s := by
  simp [actionMonomial, single_mul_single]

@[simp]
theorem actionMonomial_mul_neg [Semiring R] [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ) (r : ℝ) :
    actionMonomial R E r * actionMonomial R E (-r) = 1 := by
  rw [← actionMonomial_add, add_neg_cancel, actionMonomial_zero]

@[simp]
theorem neg_mul_actionMonomial [Semiring R] [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ) (r : ℝ) :
    actionMonomial R E (-r) * actionMonomial R E r = 1 := by
  rw [← actionMonomial_add, neg_add_cancel, actionMonomial_zero]

/-- Every real action monomial `T^r` is a unit of `NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)`,
with inverse `T^(-r)`. -/
theorem isUnit_actionMonomial [Semiring R] [AddGroup G] (E : G →+ ℝ) (r : ℝ) :
    IsUnit (actionMonomial R E r) :=
  (periodSectionUnit R (N := actionPeriod E) (.inr G ℝ) r).isUnit

/-- Every real action monomial `T^r` is homogeneous of degree `0` for `actionDegree μ`. -/
theorem actionMonomial_mem_gradeBy_zero [Semiring R] [AddZeroClass G] [AddZeroClass B]
    (E : G →+ ℝ) (μ : G →+ B) (r : ℝ) :
    actionMonomial R E r ∈ gradeBy R (actionPeriod E) (actionDegree μ) 0 := by
  simpa [actionMonomial] using
    single_mem_gradeBy (N := actionPeriod E) (actionDegree μ) ((0 : G), r) (1 : R)

/-- Multiplying by `T^r` preserves every homogeneous degree piece for `actionDegree μ`. -/
theorem actionMonomial_mul_mem_gradeBy [Semiring R] [AddMonoid G] [AddMonoid B]
    (E : G →+ ℝ) (μ : G →+ B) (r : ℝ) {b : B}
    {a : NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)}
    (ha : a ∈ gradeBy R (actionPeriod E) (actionDegree μ) b) :
    actionMonomial R E r * a ∈ gradeBy R (actionPeriod E) (actionDegree μ) b := by
  simpa using SetLike.GradedMul.mul_mem (actionMonomial_mem_gradeBy_zero E μ r) ha

/-- Multiplying by `T^r` shifts the period filtration of `NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)`
by `r`. -/
theorem actionMonomial_mul_mem_periodFiltration_iff [Ring R] [AddGroup G]
    (E : G →+ ℝ) (r C : ℝ) {a : NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)} :
    actionMonomial R E r * a ∈ periodFiltration R (actionPeriod E) (r + C) ↔
      a ∈ periodFiltration R (actionPeriod E) C := by
  simpa [actionMonomial] using
    single_mul_mem_periodFiltration_iff (N := actionPeriod E) ((0 : G), r) (1 : Rˣ) (C := C)
      (a := a)

/-- Classes of distinct degrees remain distinct in `NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)`,
even when their energies `E g₁` and `E g₂` coincide. -/
theorem single_action_ne_of_degree_ne [Zero R] [AddZeroClass G] [AddZeroClass B]
    (E : G →+ ℝ) (μ : G →+ B) {g₁ g₂ : G} (hμ : μ g₁ ≠ μ g₂) (r₁ r₂ : ℝ) {c₁ c₂ : R}
    (hc₁ : c₁ ≠ 0) :
    (single (g₁, r₁) c₁ : NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)) ≠ single (g₂, r₂) c₂ := by
  intro heq
  have hg : g₁ ≠ g₂ := fun h => hμ (congrArg μ h)
  have hp : (g₁, r₁) ≠ (g₂, r₂) := fun h => hg (congrArg Prod.fst h)
  have hc := congrArg (fun a => a.coeff (g₁, r₁)) heq
  rw [coeff_single_same, coeff_single_of_ne hp] at hc
  exact hc₁ hc

/-- The nonnegative action monomial `T^r` (`0 ≤ r`) in `nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)`. -/
def nonnegActionMonomial (R : Type*) [Ring R] {G : Type*} [AddGroup G] (E : G →+ ℝ) {r : ℝ}
    (hr : 0 ≤ r) : nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E) :=
  nonnegPeriodSection R (actionPeriod_inr E) hr

@[simp]
theorem coe_nonnegActionMonomial [Ring R] [AddGroup G] (E : G →+ ℝ) {r : ℝ} (hr : 0 ≤ r) :
    (nonnegActionMonomial R E hr : NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)) =
      actionMonomial R E r :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem nonnegActionMonomial_zero [Ring R] [AddGroup G] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    nonnegActionMonomial R E le_rfl = 1 :=
  nonnegPeriodSection_zero (actionPeriod_inr E)

@[simp]
theorem nonnegActionMonomial_add [Ring R] [AddGroup G] (E : G →+ ℝ) {r s : ℝ}
    (hr : 0 ≤ r) (hs : 0 ≤ s) :
    nonnegActionMonomial R E (add_nonneg hr hs) =
      nonnegActionMonomial R E hr * nonnegActionMonomial R E hs :=
  nonnegPeriodSection_add (actionPeriod_inr E) hr hs

theorem nonnegActionMonomial_mem_posIdeal [Ring R] [AddGroup G] (E : G →+ ℝ) {r : ℝ}
    (hr : 0 < r) : nonnegActionMonomial R E hr.le ∈ posIdeal R (actionPeriod E) :=
  nonnegPeriodSection_mem_posIdeal (actionPeriod_inr E) hr

/-- For `r > 0` over a nontrivial ring, `T^r` is not a unit of
`nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)`, in contrast to `isUnit_actionMonomial` in the localized
ring. -/
theorem not_isUnit_nonnegActionMonomial [Ring R] [Nontrivial R] [AddGroup G] (E : G →+ ℝ)
    {r : ℝ} (hr : 0 < r) : ¬ IsUnit (nonnegActionMonomial R E hr.le) :=
  not_isUnit_nonnegPeriodSection_of_pos (actionPeriod_inr E) hr

theorem nonnegActionMonomial_mem_nonnegGradeBy_zero [CommSemiring S] [Ring R] [Algebra S R]
    [AddGroup G] [AddZeroClass B] (E : G →+ ℝ) (μ : G →+ B) {r : ℝ} (hr : 0 ≤ r) :
    nonnegActionMonomial R E hr ∈ nonnegGradeBy S R (actionPeriod E) (actionDegree μ) 0 :=
  coe_mem_gradeBy_iff.1 (actionMonomial_mem_gradeBy_zero E μ r)

/-- The multiplicative submonoid `{T^r | 0 ≤ r}` of nonnegative action monomials in
`nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)`. -/
def actionSubmonoid (R : Type*) [Ring R] {G : Type*} [AddGroup G] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    Submonoid (nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)) :=
  periodSectionSubmonoid R (actionPeriod_inr E)

@[simp]
theorem mem_actionSubmonoid [Ring R] [AddGroup G] {E : G →+ ℝ}
    {a : nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)} :
    a ∈ actionSubmonoid R E ↔
      ∃ (r : ℝ) (hr : 0 ≤ r), a = nonnegActionMonomial R E hr :=
  Iff.rfl

theorem nonnegActionMonomial_mem_actionSubmonoid [Ring R] [AddGroup G] (E : G →+ ℝ) {r : ℝ}
    (hr : 0 ≤ r) : nonnegActionMonomial R E hr ∈ actionSubmonoid R E :=
  ⟨r, hr, rfl⟩

/-- `actionSubmonoid R E` equals the submonoid generated by the strictly positive action
monomials `{T^r | 0 < r}`. -/
theorem actionSubmonoid_eq_closure_pos [Ring R] [AddGroup G] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    actionSubmonoid R E =
      Submonoid.closure {a | ∃ (r : ℝ) (hr : 0 < r), a = nonnegActionMonomial R E hr.le} :=
  periodSectionSubmonoid_eq_closure_pos (actionPeriod_inr E)

/-- **Localization of the nonnegative action-weighted Novikov subring.** Localizing
`nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)` at `actionSubmonoid R E` recovers the full completed ring
`NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)`. -/
instance isLocalization_actionSubmonoid [AddCommGroup G] [CommRing R] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    IsLocalization (actionSubmonoid R E) (NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)) :=
  isLocalization_periodSectionSubmonoid (actionPeriod_inr E)

/-- The canonical ring isomorphism from `Localization (actionSubmonoid R E)` onto
`NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)`. -/
def actionLocalizationRingEquiv [AddCommGroup G] [CommRing R] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    Localization (actionSubmonoid R E) ≃+* NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E) :=
  periodSectionLocalizationRingEquiv (actionPeriod_inr E)

end Monomials

/-! ### Inclusion of base coefficients `G → G × ℝ` -/

section BaseInclusion

private theorem exists_period_rescale_inl [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    ∃ c > 0, ∀ g : G, actionPeriod E (AddMonoidHom.inl G ℝ g) = c * E g :=
  ⟨1, one_pos, fun g => by simp [actionPeriod]⟩

/-- The unital ring homomorphism embedding `NovikovSeries R G E` into
`NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)` along `g ↦ (g, 0)`. -/
def actionInlRingHom (R : Type*) [Semiring R] {G : Type*} [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    NovikovSeries R G E →+* NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E) :=
  mapRingHom (RingHom.id R) (.inl G ℝ) (exists_period_rescale_inl E)

@[simp]
theorem coeff_actionInlRingHom_zero [Semiring R] [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ)
    (a : NovikovSeries R G E) (g : G) :
    (actionInlRingHom R E a).coeff (g, 0) = a.coeff g := by
  simpa [actionInlRingHom, mapRingHom_apply] using
    coeff_map_of_injective (RingHom.id R : R →+ R) (.inl G ℝ) (exists_period_rescale_inl E)
      (Prod.mk_left_injective 0) a g

theorem coeff_actionInlRingHom_of_ne_zero [Semiring R] [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ)
    (a : NovikovSeries R G E) (g : G) {r : ℝ} (hr : r ≠ 0) :
    (actionInlRingHom R E a).coeff (g, r) = 0 := by
  rw [actionInlRingHom, mapRingHom_apply]
  refine coeff_map_eq_zero_of_notMem_range _ _ _ a ?_
  rintro ⟨g', hg'⟩
  exact hr (congrArg Prod.snd hg').symm

@[simp]
theorem actionInlRingHom_single [Semiring R] [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ) (g : G) (c : R) :
    actionInlRingHom R E (single g c) = single (g, 0) c := by
  simp [actionInlRingHom]

theorem actionInlRingHom_injective [Semiring R] [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    Injective (actionInlRingHom R E) := fun a b hab =>
  ext fun g => by
    rw [← coeff_actionInlRingHom_zero E a g, hab, coeff_actionInlRingHom_zero E b g]

@[fun_prop]
theorem continuous_actionInlRingHom [Ring R] [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    Continuous (actionInlRingHom R E) :=
  continuous_mapRingHom _ _ _

/-- `actionInlRingHom` preserves and reflects every period filtration cutoff `C`. -/
theorem actionInlRingHom_mem_periodFiltration_iff [Ring R] [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ) (C : ℝ)
    {a : NovikovSeries R G E} :
    actionInlRingHom R E a ∈ periodFiltration R (actionPeriod E) C ↔
      a ∈ periodFiltration R E C := by
  refine ⟨fun ha => mem_periodFiltration.2 fun g hg => ?_, fun ha => ?_⟩
  · rw [← coeff_actionInlRingHom_zero E a g]
    exact mem_periodFiltration.1 ha (g, 0) (by simpa using hg)
  · rw [actionInlRingHom, mapRingHom_apply]
    simpa using map_mem_periodFiltration (RingHom.id R : R →+ R) (.inl G ℝ)
      (exists_period_rescale_inl E) zero_le_one (fun g => by simp [actionPeriod]) ha

/-- `actionInlRingHom` preserves and reflects homogeneity for `μ` and `actionDegree μ`. -/
@[simp]
theorem actionInlRingHom_mem_gradeBy_iff [Semiring R] [AddMonoid G] [AddZeroClass B]
    (E : G →+ ℝ) (μ : G →+ B) (b : B) {a : NovikovSeries R G E} :
    actionInlRingHom R E a ∈ gradeBy R (actionPeriod E) (actionDegree μ) b ↔
      a ∈ gradeBy R E μ b := by
  rw [mem_gradeBy_iff, mem_gradeBy_iff]
  refine ⟨fun ha g hg => ?_, fun ha p hp => ?_⟩
  · have hp : (g, (0 : ℝ)) ∈ (actionInlRingHom R E a).support := by
      rwa [mem_support, coeff_actionInlRingHom_zero, ← mem_support]
    exact ha hp
  · rcases eq_or_ne p.2 0 with hr | hr
    · have hg : p.1 ∈ a.support := by
        rw [mem_support, ← coeff_actionInlRingHom_zero E a p.1]
        rcases p with ⟨g, r⟩
        dsimp at hr
        subst hr
        exact mem_support.1 hp
      exact ha hg
    · exact absurd (coeff_actionInlRingHom_of_ne_zero E a p.1 hr) (mem_support.1 hp)

/-- The ring homomorphism embedding `nonnegSubring R E` into `nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)`
along `g ↦ (g, 0)`. -/
def actionInlNonnegSubring (R : Type*) [Ring R] {G : Type*} [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    nonnegSubring R E →+* nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E) :=
  mapNonnegSubring (RingHom.id R) (.inl G ℝ) (exists_period_rescale_inl E)

@[simp]
theorem coe_actionInlNonnegSubring [Ring R] [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ)
    (a : nonnegSubring R E) :
    (actionInlNonnegSubring R E a : NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)) =
      actionInlRingHom R E a := by
  rw [actionInlNonnegSubring, coe_mapNonnegSubring, actionInlRingHom, mapRingHom_apply]

theorem actionInlNonnegSubring_injective [Ring R] [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    Injective (actionInlNonnegSubring R E) :=
  mapNonnegSubring_injective _ _ _ injective_id (Prod.mk_left_injective 0)

@[fun_prop]
theorem continuous_actionInlNonnegSubring [Ring R] [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    Continuous (actionInlNonnegSubring R E) :=
  continuous_mapNonnegSubring _ _ _

/-- `actionInlNonnegSubring` preserves and reflects membership in `posIdeal`; in particular,
positive degree-zero series survive the action extension. -/
theorem actionInlNonnegSubring_mem_posIdeal_iff [Ring R] [AddMonoid G] (E : G →+ ℝ)
    {a : nonnegSubring R E} :
    actionInlNonnegSubring R E a ∈ posIdeal R (actionPeriod E) ↔ a ∈ posIdeal R E := by
  rw [mem_posIdeal, mem_posIdeal]
  refine ⟨fun ha g hg => ?_, fun ha p hp => ?_⟩
  · rw [← coeff_actionInlRingHom_zero E a.1 g, ← coe_actionInlNonnegSubring]
    exact ha (g, 0) (by simpa using hg)
  · rcases eq_or_ne p.2 0 with hr | hr
    · rcases p with ⟨g, r⟩
      dsimp at hr
      subst hr
      rw [coe_actionInlNonnegSubring, coeff_actionInlRingHom_zero]
      exact ha g (by simpa using hp)
    · rw [coe_actionInlNonnegSubring]
      exact coeff_actionInlRingHom_of_ne_zero E a.1 p.1 hr

/-- `actionInlNonnegSubring` preserves and reflects homogeneity for `μ` and `actionDegree μ`. -/
theorem actionInlNonnegSubring_mem_nonnegGradeBy_iff [CommSemiring S] [Ring R] [Algebra S R]
    [AddMonoid G] [AddZeroClass B] (E : G →+ ℝ) (μ : G →+ B) (b : B) {a : nonnegSubring R E} :
    actionInlNonnegSubring R E a ∈ nonnegGradeBy S R (actionPeriod E) (actionDegree μ) b ↔
      a ∈ nonnegGradeBy S R E μ b := by
  rw [← coe_mem_gradeBy_iff, ← coe_mem_gradeBy_iff, coe_actionInlNonnegSubring,
    actionInlRingHom_mem_gradeBy_iff]

end BaseInclusion

/-! ### Energy-zero residue after real action extension -/

section ActionResidue

variable [AddGroup G] [Ring R]

/-- The additive equivalence `G ≃+ (actionPeriod E).ker` given by `g ↦ (g, -E g)`, whose inverse
projects onto the first coordinate. -/
def kerActionPeriodEquiv (E : G →+ ℝ) : G ≃+ (actionPeriod E).ker where
  toFun g := ⟨(g, -E g), by simp [actionPeriod]⟩
  invFun k := k.1.1
  left_inv _ := rfl
  right_inv := by
    rintro ⟨⟨g, r⟩, h⟩
    ext
    · rfl
    · dsimp at h ⊢
      have h0 : E g + r = 0 := h
      linarith
  map_add' g₁ g₂ := by
    ext
    · rfl
    · simp [map_add, add_comm]

@[simp]
theorem coe_kerActionPeriodEquiv (E : G →+ ℝ) (g : G) :
    (kerActionPeriodEquiv E g : G × ℝ) = (g, -E g) :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem kerActionPeriodEquiv_symm_apply (E : G →+ ℝ) (k : (actionPeriod E).ker) :
    (kerActionPeriodEquiv E).symm k = k.1.1 :=
  (rfl)

/-- The energy-zero residue homomorphism after real action extension, mapping
`nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)` onto the full group ring `AddMonoidAlgebra R G` by reading the
coefficient at `(g, -E g)`. -/
def actionResidueRingHom (R : Type*) [Ring R] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E) →+* AddMonoidAlgebra R G :=
  (AddMonoidAlgebra.mapDomainRingEquiv R (kerActionPeriodEquiv E).symm).toRingHom.comp
    (residueRingHom R (actionPeriod E))

@[simp]
theorem coeff_actionResidueRingHom (E : G →+ ℝ) (a : nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)) (g : G) :
    (actionResidueRingHom R E a).coeff g =
      (a : NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)).coeff (g, -E g) := by
  simp [actionResidueRingHom, Finsupp.equivMapDomain_apply]

/-- The group-ring section `AddMonoidAlgebra R G →+* nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)` sending
`AddMonoidAlgebra.single g r` to `single (g, -E g) r`. -/
def ofActionResidue (R : Type*) [Ring R] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    AddMonoidAlgebra R G →+* nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E) :=
  (ofKerAddMonoidAlgebra R (actionPeriod E)).comp
    (AddMonoidAlgebra.mapDomainRingEquiv R (kerActionPeriodEquiv E)).toRingHom

@[simp]
theorem ofActionResidue_single (E : G →+ ℝ) (g : G) (r : R) :
    ofActionResidue R E (AddMonoidAlgebra.single g r) =
      ⟨single (g, -E g) r, single_mem_nonnegSubring (by simp [actionPeriod]) r⟩ := by
  simp [ofActionResidue]

@[simp]
theorem actionResidueRingHom_ofActionResidue (E : G →+ ℝ) (x : AddMonoidAlgebra R G) :
    actionResidueRingHom R E (ofActionResidue R E x) = x := by
  simp only [actionResidueRingHom, ofActionResidue, RingHom.comp_apply,
    residueRingHom_ofKerAddMonoidAlgebra, RingEquiv.toRingHom_eq_coe, RingEquiv.coe_toRingHom]
  exact (AddMonoidAlgebra.mapDomainRingEquiv R (kerActionPeriodEquiv E)).symm_apply_apply x

theorem actionResidueRingHom_surjective (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    Surjective (actionResidueRingHom R E) :=
  RightInverse.surjective (actionResidueRingHom_ofActionResidue E)

@[simp]
theorem ker_actionResidueRingHom (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    RingHom.ker (actionResidueRingHom R E) = posIdeal R (actionPeriod E) := by
  ext a
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker, actionResidueRingHom, RingHom.comp_apply, RingEquiv.toRingHom_eq_coe,
    RingEquiv.coe_toRingHom, RingEquiv.map_eq_zero_iff, residueRingHom_eq_zero_iff]

/-- **Energy-zero residue after real action extension.** Quotienting
`nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)` by `posIdeal R (actionPeriod E)` gives the full group ring
`AddMonoidAlgebra R G`, via `g ↦ (g, -E g)`. -/
def quotientActionPosIdealEquiv (R : Type*) [Ring R] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    (nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E) ⧸ posIdeal R (actionPeriod E)) ≃+* AddMonoidAlgebra R G :=
  (quotientPosIdealEquiv R (actionPeriod E)).trans
    (AddMonoidAlgebra.mapDomainRingEquiv R (kerActionPeriodEquiv E).symm)

@[simp]
theorem quotientActionPosIdealEquiv_mk (E : G →+ ℝ) (a : nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)) :
    quotientActionPosIdealEquiv R E (Ideal.Quotient.mk (posIdeal R (actionPeriod E)) a) =
      actionResidueRingHom R E a := by
  simp [quotientActionPosIdealEquiv, actionResidueRingHom]

@[simp]
theorem quotientActionPosIdealEquiv_symm_apply (E : G →+ ℝ) (x : AddMonoidAlgebra R G) :
    (quotientActionPosIdealEquiv R E).symm x =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (posIdeal R (actionPeriod E)) (ofActionResidue R E x) := by
  simp [quotientActionPosIdealEquiv, ofActionResidue]

/-- The energy-zero residue isomorphism after real action extension as an `S`-algebra
equivalence. -/
def quotientActionPosIdealAlgEquiv (S R : Type*) [CommSemiring S] [Ring R] [Algebra S R]
    (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    (nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E) ⧸ posIdeal R (actionPeriod E)) ≃ₐ[S]
      AddMonoidAlgebra R G :=
  (quotientPosIdealAlgEquiv S R (actionPeriod E)).trans
    (AddMonoidAlgebra.domCongr S R (kerActionPeriodEquiv E).symm)

@[simp]
theorem quotientActionPosIdealAlgEquiv_mk [CommSemiring S] [Algebra S R] (E : G →+ ℝ)
    (a : nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)) :
    quotientActionPosIdealAlgEquiv S R E (Ideal.Quotient.mk (posIdeal R (actionPeriod E)) a) =
      actionResidueRingHom R E a := by
  simp [quotientActionPosIdealAlgEquiv, actionResidueRingHom, AddMonoidAlgebra.domCongr]

/-- The action-weighted residue map reflects units. -/
instance (E : G →+ ℝ) : IsLocalHom (actionResidueRingHom R E) where
  map_nonunit a hu := by
    rw [actionResidueRingHom, RingHom.comp_apply, RingEquiv.toRingHom_eq_coe,
      RingEquiv.coe_toRingHom, MulEquiv.isUnit_map] at hu
    exact isUnit_residueRingHom_iff.1 hu

/-- An element of `nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)` is a unit if and only if its energy-zero
residue in `AddMonoidAlgebra R G` is a unit. -/
theorem isUnit_actionResidueRingHom_iff (E : G →+ ℝ) {a : nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)} :
    IsUnit (actionResidueRingHom R E a) ↔ IsUnit a :=
  isUnit_map_iff (actionResidueRingHom R E) a

/-- The action-weighted residue map preserves the grading by `μ : G →+ B`. -/
theorem actionResidueRingHom_mem_gradeBy {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (E : G →+ ℝ) [AddZeroClass B]
    (μ : G →+ B) {b : B} {a : nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)}
    (ha : a ∈ nonnegGradeBy R R (actionPeriod E) (actionDegree μ) b) :
    actionResidueRingHom R E a ∈ AddMonoidAlgebra.gradeBy R μ b := by
  rw [AddMonoidAlgebra.mem_gradeBy_iff]
  intro g hg
  rw [Finset.mem_coe, Finsupp.mem_support_iff, coeff_actionResidueRingHom] at hg
  exact mem_nonnegGradeBy_iff.1 ha (mem_support.2 hg)

end ActionResidue

/-! ### Properness of the dense graded subalgebra for infinite degree range -/

section InfiniteDegreeProperness

/-- When the degree homomorphism `μ : G →+ B` has infinite range and `R` is nontrivial, there is a
convergent series `∑' n : ℕ, single (g n, m n) 1` in `nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)` with
pairwise distinct degrees `μ (g n)` and periods `E (g n) + m n ≥ n`, which therefore lies in no
finite sum of homogeneous pieces. -/
theorem exists_mem_nonnegSubring_notMem_iSup_nonnegGradeBy [CommSemiring S] [Ring R]
    [Nontrivial R] [Algebra S R] [AddGroup G] [AddMonoid B] (E : G →+ ℝ) (μ : G →+ B)
    (hμ : (range μ).Infinite) :
    ∃ a : nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E),
      a ∉ ⨆ b, nonnegGradeBy S R (actionPeriod E) (actionDegree μ) b := by
  classical
  let e : ℕ ↪ range μ := hμ.natEmbedding
  choose g hg using fun n : ℕ => (e n).2
  have hμg_inj : Injective fun n : ℕ => μ (g n) := fun m n hmn =>
    e.injective (Subtype.ext <| (hg m).symm.trans (hmn.trans (hg n)))
  let p : ℕ → G × ℝ := fun n => (g n, (⌈(n : ℝ) - E (g n)⌉₊ : ℝ))
  have hp_inj : Injective p := fun m n hmn =>
    hμg_inj (congrArg μ (congrArg Prod.fst hmn))
  have hp_period : ∀ n : ℕ, (n : ℝ) ≤ actionPeriod E (p n) := fun n => by
    have hceil : (n : ℝ) - E (g n) ≤ (⌈(n : ℝ) - E (g n)⌉₊ : ℝ) := Nat.le_ceil _
    dsimp [p, actionPeriod]
    linarith
  let f : ℕ → NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E) := fun n => single (p n) 1
  have hsum : Summable f := by
    rw [NonarchimedeanAddGroup.summable_iff_tendsto_cofinite_zero,
      hasBasis_nhds_zero.tendsto_right_iff]
    intro C _
    rw [eventually_cofinite]
    refine (Finset.range ⌈C⌉₊).finite_toSet.subset fun n hn => ?_
    rw [Finset.mem_coe, Finset.mem_range]
    by_contra hge
    have hle : C ≤ (n : ℝ) :=
      (Nat.le_ceil C).trans (Nat.cast_le.2 (not_lt.1 hge))
    exact hn
      (antitone_periodFiltration (hle.trans (hp_period n)) (single_mem_periodFiltration _ _))
  have hf_mem : ∀ n : ℕ, f n ∈ nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E) := fun n =>
    single_mem_nonnegSubring ((Nat.cast_nonneg n).trans (hp_period n)) 1
  let w : nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E) :=
    ⟨∑' n : ℕ, f n, tsum_mem isClosed_nonnegSubring hf_mem⟩
  have hw_coeff : ∀ k : ℕ, (w : NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)).coeff (p k) = 1 := by
    intro k
    change (∑' n : ℕ, f n).coeff (p k) = 1
    rw [hsum.tsum_eq_add_tsum_ite k, coeff_add, coeff_single_same,
      coeff_tsum_eq_zero fun n => ?_, add_zero]
    rcases eq_or_ne n k with rfl | hnk
    · simp
    · simp [hnk, f, coeff_single_of_ne (hp_inj.ne hnk.symm)]
  refine ⟨w, fun hw => ?_⟩
  have hfin := finite_image_support_of_mem_iSup_nonnegGradeBy hw
  refine (infinite_range_of_injective hμg_inj) (hfin.subset ?_)
  rintro _ ⟨k, rfl⟩
  refine ⟨p k, ?_, rfl⟩
  rw [mem_support, hw_coeff k]
  exact one_ne_zero

/-- When `μ : G →+ B` has infinite range and `R` is nontrivial, the dense graded submodule
`⨆ b, nonnegGradeBy S R (actionPeriod E) (actionDegree μ) b` is a proper submodule of
`nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)`. -/
theorem iSup_nonnegGradeBy_actionDegree_ne_top [CommSemiring S] [Ring R] [Nontrivial R]
    [Algebra S R] [AddGroup G] [AddMonoid B] (E : G →+ ℝ) (μ : G →+ B)
    (hμ : (range μ).Infinite) :
    ⨆ b, nonnegGradeBy S R (actionPeriod E) (actionDegree μ) b ≠ ⊤ := by
  intro htop
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := exists_mem_nonnegSubring_notMem_iSup_nonnegGradeBy (S := S) (R := R) E μ hμ
  exact ha (htop ▸ Submodule.mem_top)

/-- When `μ : G →+ B` has infinite range and `R` is nontrivial, the canonical graded algebra
homomorphism `DirectSum.coeAlgHom` into `nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)` is not surjective,
even though its range is dense (`denseRange_coeAlgHom_nonnegGradeBy`). -/
theorem not_surjective_coeAlgHom_actionDegree [CommSemiring S] [Ring R] [Nontrivial R]
    [Algebra S R] [AddGroup G] [DecidableEq B] [AddMonoid B] (E : G →+ ℝ) (μ : G →+ B)
    (hμ : (range μ).Infinite) :
    ¬ Surjective (DirectSum.coeAlgHom (nonnegGradeBy S R (actionPeriod E) (actionDegree μ))) := by
  intro hsurj
  refine iSup_nonnegGradeBy_actionDegree_ne_top (S := S) (R := R) E μ hμ ?_
  rw [Submodule.iSup_eq_toSubmodule_range, eq_top_iff]
  rintro a -
  exact hsurj a

end InfiniteDegreeProperness

end ActionExtension

/-! ### Action-field specialization and the real Novikov ring -/

section ActionSpecialization

variable {R k G : Type*}

private theorem exists_period_rescale_actionPeriod [AddZeroClass G] (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    ∃ c > 0, ∀ p : G × ℝ, (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ) (actionPeriod E p) = c * actionPeriod E p :=
  ⟨1, one_pos, fun _ => (one_mul _).symm⟩

/-- **Action specialization.** Pushforward of action-weighted Novikov series along
`actionPeriod E : G × ℝ →+ ℝ` and a unital coefficient homomorphism `ρ : R →+* k`, summing the
mapped coefficients along each constant-energy slice `E g + r = t`. -/
def actionSpecialization [Semiring R] [Semiring k] [AddMonoid G] (ρ : R →+* k)
    (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E) →+* NovikovSeries k ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ) :=
  mapRingHom ρ (actionPeriod E) (exists_period_rescale_actionPeriod E)

theorem coeff_actionSpecialization [Semiring R] [Semiring k] [AddMonoid G] (ρ : R →+* k)
    (E : G →+ ℝ) (a : NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)) (t : ℝ) :
    (actionSpecialization ρ E a).coeff t = ∑ᶠ p ∈ actionPeriod E ⁻¹' {t}, ρ (a.coeff p) := by
  rw [actionSpecialization, mapRingHom_apply, coeff_map]
  rfl

@[simp]
theorem actionSpecialization_single [Semiring R] [Semiring k] [AddMonoid G] (ρ : R →+* k)
    (E : G →+ ℝ) (g : G) (r : ℝ) (c : R) :
    actionSpecialization ρ E (single (g, r) c) = single (E g + r) (ρ c) := by
  simp [actionSpecialization]

@[simp]
theorem actionSpecialization_actionMonomial [Semiring R] [Semiring k] [AddMonoid G]
    (ρ : R →+* k) (E : G →+ ℝ) (r : ℝ) :
    actionSpecialization ρ E (actionMonomial R E r) = single r 1 := by
  simp [actionMonomial]

@[fun_prop]
theorem continuous_actionSpecialization [Ring R] [Ring k] [AddMonoid G] (ρ : R →+* k)
    (E : G →+ ℝ) : Continuous (actionSpecialization ρ E) :=
  continuous_mapRingHom _ _ _

/-- The action specialization sends the period neighbourhood `U_C` into `U'_C`. -/
theorem actionSpecialization_mem_periodFiltration [Ring R] [Ring k] [AddMonoid G]
    (ρ : R →+* k) (E : G →+ ℝ) {C : ℝ} {a : NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)}
    (ha : a ∈ periodFiltration R (actionPeriod E) C) :
    actionSpecialization ρ E a ∈ periodFiltration k (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ) C := by
  rw [actionSpecialization, mapRingHom_apply]
  simpa using map_mem_periodFiltration (ρ : R →+ k) (actionPeriod E)
    (exists_period_rescale_actionPeriod E) zero_le_one (fun _ => (one_mul _).symm) ha

/-- The restriction of `actionSpecialization` to the nonnegative subrings. -/
def nonnegActionSpecialization [Ring R] [Ring k] [AddMonoid G] (ρ : R →+* k) (E : G →+ ℝ) :
    nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E) →+* nonnegSubring k (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ) :=
  mapNonnegSubring ρ (actionPeriod E) (exists_period_rescale_actionPeriod E)

@[simp]
theorem coe_nonnegActionSpecialization [Ring R] [Ring k] [AddMonoid G] (ρ : R →+* k)
    (E : G →+ ℝ) (a : nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E)) :
    (nonnegActionSpecialization ρ E a : NovikovSeries k ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)) =
      actionSpecialization ρ E a := by
  rw [nonnegActionSpecialization, coe_mapNonnegSubring, actionSpecialization, mapRingHom_apply]

@[fun_prop]
theorem continuous_nonnegActionSpecialization [Ring R] [Ring k] [AddMonoid G] (ρ : R →+* k)
    (E : G →+ ℝ) : Continuous (nonnegActionSpecialization ρ E) :=
  continuous_mapNonnegSubring _ _ _

/-- `actionSpecialization ρ E` is the unique ring homomorphism out of the localized ring
`NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E)` extending `nonnegActionSpecialization ρ E`. -/
theorem eq_actionSpecialization_of_comp_nonneg [AddCommGroup G] [CommRing R] [Ring k]
    (ρ : R →+* k) (E : G →+ ℝ)
    {φ : NovikovSeries R (G × ℝ) (actionPeriod E) →+* NovikovSeries k ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)}
    (hφ : ∀ a : nonnegSubring R (actionPeriod E),
      φ a = nonnegActionSpecialization ρ E a) :
    φ = actionSpecialization ρ E :=
  IsLocalization.ringHom_ext (actionSubmonoid R E) <|
    RingHom.ext fun a => (hφ a).trans (coe_nonnegActionSpecialization ρ E a)

/-! ### The real Novikov ring and field -/

/-- The multiplicative submonoid `{single r 1 | 0 ≤ r}` of nonnegative real monomials in
`nonnegSubring R (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)`. -/
def realActionSubmonoid (R : Type*) [Ring R] :
    Submonoid (nonnegSubring R (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)) :=
  periodSectionSubmonoid R (N := AddMonoidHom.id ℝ) (ι := AddMonoidHom.id ℝ) fun _ => rfl

/-- `realActionSubmonoid R` equals the submonoid generated by the strictly positive real
monomials `{single r 1 | 0 < r}`. -/
theorem realActionSubmonoid_eq_closure_pos (R : Type*) [Ring R] :
    realActionSubmonoid R =
      Submonoid.closure {a : nonnegSubring R (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ) |
        ∃ (r : ℝ) (hr : 0 < r),
          a = ⟨single r 1, single_mem_nonnegSubring hr.le 1⟩} :=
  periodSectionSubmonoid_eq_closure_pos (N := AddMonoidHom.id ℝ) (ι := AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)
    fun _ => rfl

/-- Localizing `nonnegSubring R (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)` at the nonnegative (equivalently, strictly
positive) real monomials recovers `NovikovSeries R ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)`. -/
instance isLocalization_realActionSubmonoid (R : Type*) [CommRing R] :
    IsLocalization (realActionSubmonoid R) (NovikovSeries R ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)) :=
  isLocalization_periodSectionSubmonoid (N := AddMonoidHom.id ℝ) (ι := AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)
    fun _ => rfl

/-- Over a field `k`, the real Novikov ring `NovikovSeries k ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)` is a field. -/
theorem isField_realNovikovSeries (k : Type*) [Field k] :
    IsField (NovikovSeries k ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)) :=
  isField_iff.2 ⟨Field.toIsField k, injective_id⟩

/-- A nonzero series in `NovikovSeries R ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)` has nonzero coefficient at its
order `b.order`. -/
theorem coeff_order_ne_zero_of_id [Zero R] {b : NovikovSeries R ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)}
    (hb : b ≠ 0) : b.coeff b.order ≠ 0 := by
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hord⟩ := exists_coeff_ne_zero_and_period_eq_order hb
  exact (hord : t = b.order) ▸ ht

/-- **Leading-term factorization in the real Novikov division ring.** Over a division ring `D`,
every nonzero series `b` in `NovikovSeries D ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)` factors at its least exponent
`b.order` as `single b.order (b.coeff b.order) * (1 + a)` with
`a ∈ posIdeal D (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)` and `1 + a` a unit of `nonnegSubring D (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)`
(inverted by the geometric series of `-a`). -/
theorem exists_posIdeal_eq_single_order_mul_one_add {D : Type*} [DivisionRing D]
    {b : NovikovSeries D ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ)} (hb : b ≠ 0) :
    ∃ a : nonnegSubring D (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ),
      a ∈ posIdeal D (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ) ∧
        b = single b.order (b.coeff b.order) *
          (1 + (a : NovikovSeries D ℝ (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ))) ∧
        IsUnit (1 + a) := by
  obtain ⟨t, r, c, hc, hb_eq⟩ := exists_single_mul_one_sub_of_injective injective_id hb
  have hrc : b.coeff t = r := by
    simp [hb_eq, coeff_single_mul, coeff_sub, coeff_one, mem_posIdeal.1 hc 0 le_rfl]
  have ht : b.order = t := order_eq_of_isLeast
    ⟨⟨t, mem_support.2 (hrc.symm ▸ r.ne_zero), rfl⟩,
      fun s ⟨u, hu, hus⟩ => not_lt.1 fun hut => by
        have hus' : u = s := hus
        subst hus'
        have hne : -t + u ≠ 0 := by linarith
        have hle : (AddMonoidHom.id ℝ) (-t + u) ≤ 0 := by change -t + u ≤ 0; linarith
        simp [mem_support, hb_eq, coeff_single_mul, coeff_sub, coeff_one, hne,
          mem_posIdeal.1 hc (-t + u) hle] at hu⟩
  refine ⟨-c, neg_mem hc, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [ht, hrc, Subring.coe_neg, ← sub_eq_add_neg]
    exact hb_eq
  · rw [← sub_eq_add_neg]
    exact isUnit_one_sub_of_mem_posIdeal hc

end ActionSpecialization

